the sense of the Adams inequality. By using a minimax principle based on the
homotopy stable family, we obtain that the above problem admits at least one
ground state normalized solution.
  As for the signing of the ground state normalized solution, we sign the
ground state normalized solution for the following biharmonic Choquard type
problem \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \displaystyle\min_{u\in H^2(\mathbb{R}^4)}\Phi(u),
  \end{array}
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} where \begin{align*}
  \Phi(u)=\frac{1}{2}\|\Delta u\|^2_{2}+\frac{\beta}{4}\|\nabla u\|^2_{2}+
\frac{1}{\mu+2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}|\Delta u|^{1+\mu}dx+\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}|\Delta
u|dx,
  \end{align*} and give a characterization of the minimizer of $\Phi$.
  Finally, we prove the existence and uniqueness of the extremal function of the
sharp Strauss type inequality for the biharmonic operator.
